                <pb facs="0478" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg376"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5137: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Nicaragua</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-11T21:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11,
                                1927—9 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>192. Your 326, November 11, 10 a.m. communicated to Colonel Stimson. He did not
                    have his records with him but stated he clearly remembers when discussing matter
                    with President Diaz and Cuadra Pasos that they stated that they wished to
                    contest elections in one province, which he thinks was Esteli. In view of this
                    and the conditions set forth by you Department sees no reason why Conservatives
                    should refrain from contesting this election.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
